# Security headers. Applied automatically by Cloudflare Pages and Netlify.
# GitHub Pages ignores this file; if the site stays on GitHub Pages behind
# Cloudflare, add the same headers once as a Cloudflare Transform Rule
# (Rules > Transform Rules > Modify Response Header). See README.md "Security".
#
# Every page carries its own full policy in a <meta> tag (the contact and
# subscribe pages allow their forms, the app its script). The header adds only
# what a meta tag cannot, frame-ancestors (the site can never be framed by
# another site), and rules that hold for every page. Browsers apply both
# policies, so a stricter header (form-action 'none', for one) would break the
# contact and newsletter forms.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-XSS-Protection: 0
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests

/data/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
